pi-sandbox: enable Sandbox Runtime weaker nested sandbox mode

@erichll/pi-sandbox 0.24.0 builds the Sandbox Runtime config with only
filesystem and network keys, so every sandbox requests a fresh procfs
(--proc /proc).  An unprivileged container refuses that remount, so each
sandboxed Bash command dies with:

    bwrap: Can't mount proc on /newroot/proc: Operation not permitted

bubblewrap 0.8 closes every route to fixing that with privileges for a
non-root caller: setuid mode was removed upstream and the binary hard-dies
when a non-zero real uid has capabilities ("Unexpected capabilities but not
setuid").  Running the agent as root is the only capability route, which this
deployment rejects.

Sandbox Runtime already documents the supported answer for this environment:
enableWeakerNestedSandbox substitutes "--bind /proc /proc" (see
linux-sandbox-utils.js, "weaker nested sandbox mode for Docker environments").
pi-sandbox never passes the flag and its own config parser rejects unknown
keys, so the patch adds it to toSandboxRuntimeConfig(), gated by
PI_SANDBOX_WEAKER_NESTED (default on; set to "off" when not nested).

Applied by the Dockerfile after npm install.  Re-verify on every pi-sandbox
version bump: the build fails if this hunk no longer applies.

--- a/src/policy.ts
+++ b/src/policy.ts
@@ -303,5 +303,11 @@
       allowAllUnixSockets: policy.network.allowAllUnixSockets,
       allowUnixSockets: [...policy.network.allowUnixSockets],
     },
+    // work image patch: this image always runs nested inside a container, where
+    // an unprivileged bwrap cannot remount a fresh procfs (--proc /proc).  Bind
+    // the container's /proc instead via Sandbox Runtime's documented weaker
+    // nested mode.  Set PI_SANDBOX_WEAKER_NESTED=off to restore --proc when
+    // running the sandbox without container nesting.
+    enableWeakerNestedSandbox: process.env.PI_SANDBOX_WEAKER_NESTED !== "off",
   };
 }
